{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4369870","formula":"C₁₃H₃₀Br₂N₂","hill":"C13H30Br2N2","elements":["H","C","N","Br"],"composition":{"C":13.0,"H":30.0,"N":2.0,"Br":2.0},"names":{"en":"Polybrene","ru":"Полибрен"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hexadimethrine bromide (commercial brand name Polybrene) is a cationic polymer with several uses. In research, it is primarily used to increase the efficiency of transduction of certain cells with viruses (such as retrovirus or lentivirus) in cell culture. Hexadimethrine bromide acts by neutralizing the charge repulsion between virions and sialic acid on the cell surface.","ru":"Полибрен (гексадиметрина бромид) — катионный полимер, используемый для повышения эффективности заражения ретровирусами эукариотических клеток в клеточной культуре. Полибрен нейтрализует заряды отталкивания между вирионами и сиаловой кислотой на поверхности клетки.. Так же используется при секвенировании белков."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":24769,"mass":374.2,"charge":0,"smiles":"CN(C)CCCCCCN(C)C.C(CBr)CBr","inchikey":"KZKAYEGOIJEWQB-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1,3-dibromopropane;N,N,N',N'-tetramethylhexane-1,6-diamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"24769","atoms":47,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-2.804,"y":-1.387,"z":1.361,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.823,"y":-0.614,"z":0.118,"el":"N"},{"x":-4.056,"y":-0.901,"z":-0.62,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.653,"y":-0.897,"z":-0.731,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.334,"y":-0.397,"z":-0.125,"el":"C"},{"x":0.828,"y":-0.583,"z":-1.105,"el":"C"},{"x":2.148,"y":-0.1,"z":-0.501,"el":"C"},{"x":3.306,"y":-0.278,"z":-1.488,"el":"C"},{"x":4.643,"y":0.257,"z":-0.95,"el":"C"},{"x":5.085,"y":-0.357,"z":0.313,"el":"N"},{"x":5.431,"y":-1.77,"z":0.145,"el":"C"},{"x":6.236,"y":0.373,"z":0.85,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.705,"y":-1.187,"z":1.953,"el":"H"},{